A16_SMSS_72_M016936_045                                                       
                                                                              
Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D-4                             
                                                                              
Pre-Flight Penetration Calibration Table                                      
                                                                              
This handwritten table gives the pre-flight penetration calibration data      
for the Apollo 16 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) flight unit,       
lunar drum S/N 2003.  The tests were done using deadweight loading on 19      
April 1972.  The upper part of the table gives the penetration calibration    
as cathetometer reading in centimeters for each index measured.  The same     
value was used for each index.  The lower part of the table gives average     
delta (difference between the ref., 89.87, and the other readings across      
the top of the chart), equivalent inches and equivalent centimeters to be     
used in the calibration.                                                      
                                                                              
